  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing an energy-sustainable shoe village in Hebron for the decarbonization and sustainable development of the footwear value chain in the State of Palestine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project builds on the #Upgrading of the footwear value chain in Hebron district# Project, funded by AICS and implemented by UNIDO from May 2018 to December 2019 in partnership with the Ministry of National Economy, the Hebron Chamber of Commerce and Industry, and the Federation of Leather and Shoe Industry of Palestine. Excellent results and sustainability of the provided services were achieved by the team on the ground and maintained through the specialized private sector associations. Building on these results, this Project intends to address the criticality of the energy situation for industries through established and dedicated support in terms of sustainable technology and infrastructure for enabling development and scaling up of capacities for boosting competitiveness and linkages between sectors and the market..</narrative>
  </description>
